<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<beans xmlns="http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="
        http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans/spring-beans.xsd">

	<bean id="db" class="com.nit.beans.DummyBean" />

	<bean id="calculator" class="com.nit.beans.Calculator">
		<constructor-arg name="a" value="200" />
		<constructor-arg name="c" value="Nazeer" />
	</bean>
	
	<bean id="mb" class="com.nit.beans.MyBean" />
	
</beans>

<!-- 
Important:
BeanFactory container performs lazy loading or it can NOT pre-instantiate spring beans with singleton scope.
when you run this application you don't see DummyBean and MyBean objects getting created by container unless
1. you invoke them by getBean('db') or getBean('mb');
2. configure them as dependent beans to any target bean then they will be instantiated.

If we are using ApplicationContext Container which has pre-instantiation capability for singleton beans 
these two beans will be pre-instantiated, no need do above 1,2 points.
 -->